      {
        "id": 126878,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-12T01:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But in terms of correctness, those are two completely separate sentences, and I would expect them to happen separately when evaluated by the App.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>[quote=Spiff's FAQ]</p>\n<div>“incidental contact”</div><div>this card says, “knife deals each target 1 energy damage.</div><div>knyfe may deal any target dealt damage this way an additional</div><div>1 energy damage”. this card works in a similar way to</div><div>tachyon’s “hypersonic assault”, in that the second sentence</div><div>isn’t meant to be a separate step, it just acts to modify the</div><div>first sentence.</div><div>So the proper way to deal with this card is to deal each</div><div>target 1 energy damage, and each time you do, decide whether</div><div>or not to deal an additional 1 energy damage before moving</div><div>on to the next target.</div><div>[/quote]</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>[quote=Spiff's FAQ]</div><div><div>“hypersonic assault”</div><div>this card deals each non-hero target 1 sonic damage. any</div><div>target dealt damage this way cannot deal damage until the</div><div>start of your next turn.</div><div>some cards deal damage in response to having been damaged</div><div>(ambuscade’s “sonic mines” for example), and because the two</div><div>sentences on “hypersonic assault” are separated, it may seem</div><div>like the order of operations would go like this – tachyon</div><div>deals damage, the target card deals its damage back, and then</div><div>the second sentence kicks in saying that the targeted card</div><div>can’t deal any damage (now that it’s too late). However, that</div><div>second sentence is just meant to modify the damage being</div><div>done by the first sentence and there isn’t any separation</div><div>between the two operations. so the correct order would be - - tachyon deals damage, which causes any target damaged to</div><div>not be able to deal their damage, then when the targeted card</div><div>tries to deal its response damage, it can’t.</div><div>[/quote]</div></div>\n&nbsp;",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:24.351Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
