        "raw": "[quote=\"AlexxKay\"]\n\nBut in terms of correctness, those are two completely separate sentences, and I would expect them to happen separately when evaluated by the App.&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\n[quote=Spiff&#39;s FAQ]\n<div>&ldquo;incidental contact&rdquo;</div><div>this card says, &ldquo;knife deals each target 1 energy damage.</div><div>knyfe may deal any target dealt damage this way an additional</div><div>1 energy damage&rdquo;. this card works in a similar way to</div><div>tachyon&rsquo;s &ldquo;hypersonic assault&rdquo;, in that the second sentence</div><div>isn&rsquo;t meant to be a separate step, it just acts to modify the</div><div>first sentence.</div><div>So the proper way to deal with this card is to deal each</div><div>target 1 energy damage, and each time you do, decide whether</div><div>or not to deal an additional 1 energy damage before moving</div><div>on to the next target.</div><div>[/quote]</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>[quote=Spiff&#39;s FAQ]</div><div><div>&ldquo;hypersonic assault&rdquo;</div><div>this card deals each non-hero target 1 sonic damage. any</div><div>target dealt damage this way cannot deal damage until the</div><div>start of your next turn.</div><div>some cards deal damage in response to having been damaged</div><div>(ambuscade&rsquo;s &ldquo;sonic mines&rdquo; for example), and because the two</div><div>sentences on &ldquo;hypersonic assault&rdquo; are separated, it may seem</div><div>like the order of operations would go like this &ndash; tachyon</div><div>deals damage, the target card deals its damage back, and then</div><div>the second sentence kicks in saying that the targeted card</div><div>can&rsquo;t deal any damage (now that it&rsquo;s too late). However, that</div><div>second sentence is just meant to modify the damage being</div><div>done by the first sentence and there isn&rsquo;t any separation</div><div>between the two operations. so the correct order would be - - tachyon deals damage, which causes any target damaged to</div><div>not be able to deal their damage, then when the targeted card</div><div>tries to deal its response damage, it can&rsquo;t.</div><div>[/quote]</div></div>\n&nbsp;\n",
